answer:
According to Article 2.60 of the Collective Agreement, a Joint Consultative Committee for the Administration of the Collective Agreement shall be formed and composed of three representatives from each party. The parties agree that this committee will attempt to maintain cooperation and mutual respect between them, facilitate better working relationships, and discuss matters of concern.

The composition of the committee is as follows: 

* The President of the Union and the Vice-President, Academic and Provost or their respective designates; 
* One officer of LUFA; 
* One Dean appointed by the Vice-President, Academic and Provost; 
* And one appointee from each party. (Collective Agreement 2017-2020, page 2)

The committee shall meet at least twice a year, in November and February, and at other times as deemed necessary or useful by mutual agreement of the parties. The chair of the committee will alternate between a representative of the Employer and a representative of the Union, and is responsible for preparing agendas and minutes of meetings. (Collective Agreement 2017-2020, pages 2-3)

The Joint Consultative Committee shall not have the power to add to or modify the terms of this Collective Agreement. (Collective Agreement 2017-2020, page 3)

