answer:
According to Article 8.80 - Policy and Procedures in the Event of Death, the following are the procedures for beneficiaries:

1. The beneficiary must contact the Pension and Benefits Officer in the Personnel Office.
2. If within seven (7) days the University has not been contacted by the beneficiary, the University shall make every reasonable effort to contact the beneficiary.

Additionally, the following documents will be required to request payment of life insurance proceeds:

(i) The beneficiary must complete a Statement required by the insurance carrier as well as provide her/his Social Insurance Number;
(ii) The notice of the Employee's death that appeared in the Obituary Notices;
(iii) A Death Certificate;
(iv) The last insurance certificate that was issued to the faculty Member.

The life insurance proceeds are usually paid within one (1) month.

