answer:
According to the Laurentian University Faculty Association collective agreement (Mediation Term Sheet, April 7, 2021), the term "scholarly activity" is defined on page 3 of the document as follows:

(a) Research directed towards a contribution to knowledge, and the dissemination of its results;
(b) Participation in those academic activities that contribute to the enhancement, creation and dissemination of knowledge;
(c) [This part is missing from the provided context, but other sources suggest it may involve creating scholarly work.]

Regarding definitions related to intellectual patents and copyright, there is a committee established to define these terms (Article 39.02, Mediation Term Sheet, April 7, 2021). This committee meets at least twice annually to conduct such business as referred to it, consider strategies for marketing inventions, improvements or discoveries, and recommend proposals for modifications or changes in the patents and copyright articles of this Collective Agreement (Article 39.02, Mediation Term Sheet, April 7, 2021).

It is also worth noting that there are certain specific duties related to scholarly activity that may be assigned by the Dean/University Librarian on an ad-hoc basis to ensure a good and proper functioning of the University (Context, not specified page number). However, there are also duties (D), (E), and (F) that are undertaken voluntarily by the member. The parties recognize that acknowledging Indigenous knowledge requires applying a definition of Indigenous knowledge for the application of rights, duties, responsibilities, and obligations (Context, not specified page number).

